/* ============================================================================
   Hereditary Hemorrhagic Telangiectasia (HHT / Osler-Weber-Rendu)
   Hereditary Hemorrhagic Telangiectasia — mechanistic QSP map

   ORGANISING THESIS
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   HHT is usually drawn as "loss of a brake on angiogenesis".  That picture
   cannot explain why the same germline lesion produces a 1 mm punctate
   telangiectasia in the nose and a 3 cm arteriovenous malformation in the
   liver, nor why anti-angiogenic drugs shrink the first and only dent the
   second.  This map is built on a different claim.

   CLAIM 1 — ALK1/ENG/SMAD4 IS THE ENDOTHELIAL SHEAR SET-POINT CONTROLLER,
             AND LOSING IT INVERTS THE SIGN OF A FEEDBACK LOOP.
     In normal endothelium a rise in wall shear stress drives INWARD
     remodelling: the lumen narrows and shear returns to its set point.  That
     is a NEGATIVE feedback and it is transduced by BMP9/BMP10-ALK1-endoglin
     through SMAD1/5/8 (PMID 27646277, 32078368, 37490341, 38727966).
     A two-hit lesion has no pathway left, so the same rise in shear now drives
     OUTWARD remodelling.  One line of the model carries it (cluster 5):

            REMOD = KSH * g(WSS) * (1 - 2*pSMAD_rel)

     pSMAD_rel = 1 (intact)      -> term NEGATIVE -> inward, self-limiting
     pSMAD_rel ~ 0.03 (2-hit)    -> term POSITIVE -> outward, self-amplifying

     The disease is therefore not "too much angiogenesis".  It is a control
     loop running with the wrong sign.

   CLAIM 2 — WALL SHEAR IS NOT MONOTONE IN LUMEN SIZE, AND THAT IS WHAT
             SEPARATES A TELANGIECTASIA FROM AN AVM.
     Q = dP/(R_feeder + R_lesion) with R_lesion ~ S^-4, so
            WSS ~ Q/S^3 ~ S / (1 + (S/S_feeder)^4)
     Shear RISES while the lesion is the limiting resistance and FALLS once the
     FEEDING VESSEL is.  A nasal mucosal ectasia is fed by an arteriole: shear
     saturates at a small calibre, the positive branch is capped below the
     inward-remodelling sink, and the lesion has a STABLE calibre that a drug
     can pull back.  A hepatic or pulmonary shunt is fed by a conducting
     artery: shear never saturates and the lesion runs to a floor no
     anti-angiogenic dose can go below.  Same equation, two basins.

   CLAIM 3 — ANAEMIA IS AN INPUT TO LESION GROWTH, NOT ONLY ITS OUTPUT.
     Hb falls -> cardiac output rises to defend O2 delivery -> perfusion
     pressure and wall shear rise -> outward remodelling -> larger lesions ->
     more bleeding -> Hb falls.  The loop is closed on this map (cluster 16 ->
     cluster 5).  Correcting the anaemia is therefore not purely supportive: it
     withdraws the mechanical drive that enlarges the lesions.

   CLAIM 4 — THE CLINICALLY DECISIVE VARIABLE IS A FLUX BALANCE, NOT A SCORE.
     Iron in blood = 0.0347 x Hb[g/dL] mg per mL.  Steady state requires
            absorbed - obligatory = 0.0347 x Hb x blood-loss rate
     which inverts to a MAXIMUM BLOOD LOSS each iron strategy can sustain
     (cluster 15): 8.4 mL/d on diet alone, 17.8 mL/d on oral supplements
     (hepcidin-capped, so 200 mg/d buys nothing over 65 mg/d), 88 mL/d on
     monthly IV iron.  Benefit in HHT is therefore THRESHOLD-LIKE in a way
     the continuous Epistaxis Severity Score cannot show: a drug that halves
     bleeding helps enormously if it crosses the ceiling and barely at all if
     it does not.

   WHAT THE DRUGS ACTUALLY TOUCH (clusters 17-21)
     bevacizumab   VEGF-A ligand           -> angiogenic drive only
     pazopanib     VEGFR2 (+ PDGFRbeta)    -> drive, MINUS a mural-cell penalty
     pomalidomide  PDGF-B / mural cells    -> fragility, not calibre
     tranexamic    plasmin                 -> clot only; cannot touch a lesion
     iron / RBC    the flux balance        -> and, via CLAIM 3, the shear drive
     embolisation  removes the flow itself -> the only lever on an AVM

   Bold border = ODE state variable in hht_mrgsolve_model_en.R
   ============================================================================ */

digraph HHT_QSP {
    graph [rankdir=TB, splines=spline, overlap=false, nodesep=0.26,
           ranksep=0.52, compound=true, concentrate=false,
           fontname="NanumGothic", fontsize=13, labelloc="t",
           bgcolor="white", pad=0.4,
           label=<<b>Hereditary Hemorrhagic Telangiectasia (HHT) — Quantitative Systems Pharmacology Map</b><br/>
<i>Hereditary Hemorrhagic Telangiectasia · Osler-Weber-Rendu · QSP map</i><br/>
<font point-size="11">ALK1/ENG/SMAD4 are regulators of the endothelial <b>shear stress set point</b> — lose them and the <b>sign of the feedback flips</b>, so inward remodelling becomes outward remodelling</font><br/>
<font point-size="11">Shear stress does not rise monotonically with lumen size (the feeder vessel limit) — which is why nasal lesions can be reversed with drugs and hepatic · pulmonary AVMs cannot</font><br/>
<font point-size="11">Anaemia is not only an outcome but an <b>input</b>: Hb↓ → cardiac output↑ → shear stress↑ → lesion enlargement → bleeding↑</font><br/>
<font point-size="11">Clinical benefit is not continuous but a <b>threshold</b>: whether the iron absorption ceiling (17.8 mL/day on oral iron) is exceeded is what decides transfusion dependence</font><br/>
<font point-size="10">214 nodes · 22 mechanism clusters · 50 ODE states</font>>];

    node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="NanumGothic",
          fontsize=10, margin="0.10,0.055", penwidth=1.0, color="#555555"];
    edge [fontname="NanumGothic", fontsize=8, arrowsize=0.65,
          color="#666666", penwidth=1.0];

    /* ---------- legend ------------------------------------------------ */
    subgraph cluster_legend {
        label=<<b>Legend</b>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#fafafa"; color="#bbbbbb"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=plaintext, style="", fillcolor="none", fontsize=9];
        LEG [label=<<table border="0" cellborder="0" cellspacing="1">
<tr><td align="left"><font color="#1a7f37">━━▶</font></td><td align="left">activation / promotion</td></tr>
<tr><td align="left"><font color="#c0392b">━━⊣</font></td><td align="left">inhibition / blockade</td></tr>
<tr><td align="left"><font color="#8e44ad">┅┅▶</font></td><td align="left">drug action</td></tr>
<tr><td align="left"><font color="#e67e22">━━▶</font></td><td align="left">clinical readout</td></tr>
<tr><td align="left"><font color="#2471a3">━━▶</font></td><td align="left">mass flux</td></tr>
<tr><td align="left"><font color="#b03a2e"><b>━━▶</b></font></td><td align="left">mechanical feedback</td></tr>
<tr><td align="left"><b>bold border</b></td><td align="left">ODE state variable</td></tr>
</table>>];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 1. Genes · germline variant · somatic second hit                     *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_gene {
        label=<<b>1. Genotype · heterozygosity · somatic second hit</b><br/><font point-size="9">germline haploinsufficiency + somatic second hit (PMID 39299239)</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#eef6fd"; color="#a9cce3"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#e8f4fd"];

        G_ENG    [label="ENG (endoglin) 9q34\nHHT1 · ~53% of all cases\nco-receptor CD105"];
        G_ACVRL1 [label="ACVRL1 (ALK1) 12q13\nHHT2 · ~39% of all cases\ntype I receptor kinase"];
        G_SMAD4  [label="SMAD4 18q21\nJP-HHT overlap syndrome ~2%\nwith juvenile polyposis", fillcolor="#fdf2e9"];
        G_GDF2   [label="GDF2 (BMP9) 10q11\nultra-rare · HHT5 phenotype", fillcolor="#fdf2e9"];
        G_UNK    [label="No gene identified ~2-5%\nCuraçao clinical diagnosis"];
        HAPLO    [label="Germline haploinsufficiency\none functional allele (GD=0.5)\nthe whole systemic endothelium is sensitised", penwidth=2.2, fillcolor="#d6eaf8"];
        SOMHIT   [label="Somatic second hit\nbiallelic loss in a local clone\n(PMID 39299239 · 41162588)", fillcolor="#fadbd8", penwidth=2.2];
        TRIGGER  [label="Angiogenic trigger\ntrauma · infection · inflammation · UV\n(why lesions are focal and discontinuous)"];
        FIELD    [label="Pre-lesional endothelial field\nGD=0.5 · function retained\n(awaiting the second hit)", penwidth=2.2];
        LESEC    [label="Lesional endothelium\nGD_LES ≈ 0.055 (effectively non-functional)\nloss of the pSMAD pathway", penwidth=2.2, fillcolor="#fadbd8"];
        MODGENE  [label="Modifier gene load ANGF\nVEGF-axis polymorphisms · phenotypic variability\n(same variant, different severity)"];

        G_ENG -> HAPLO [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        G_ACVRL1 -> HAPLO [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        G_SMAD4 -> HAPLO [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        G_GDF2 -> HAPLO [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        G_UNK -> HAPLO [style=dashed];
        HAPLO -> FIELD [color="#1a7f37"];
        FIELD -> SOMHIT [color="#2471a3"];
        TRIGGER -> SOMHIT [color="#1a7f37", label="conversion probability"];
        SOMHIT -> LESEC [color="#c0392b", penwidth=1.6];
        MODGENE -> FIELD [color="#1a7f37", style=dashed];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 2. BMP9/BMP10 - ALK1 - endoglin receptor complex                     *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_recept {
        label=<<b>2. BMP9/BMP10 — ALK1 — endoglin receptor complex</b><br/><font point-size="9">circulating vascular quiescence factor (PMID 18309101)</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#eafaf1"; color="#a9dfbf"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#e8f8f0"];

        BMP9     [label="BMP9 (GDF2) circulating ligand\nfrom hepatic stellate cells · 2-12 ng/mL\nvascular quiescence factor", penwidth=2.2];
        BMP10    [label="BMP10\nfrom the right atrium · equipotent at ALK1\n(PMID 36348215)"];
        PROD_BMP [label="BMP9 prodomain-bound form\nactive/inactive equilibrium"];
        ENG_PROT [label="Endoglin (CD105)\ntype I membrane co-receptor\nligand presentation · signal amplification", penwidth=2.2];
        SENG     [label="Soluble endoglin (sENG)\nMMP cleavage product · ligand scavenging\n(PMID 31431534)", fillcolor="#fdedec"];
        ALK1     [label="ALK1 (ACVRL1)\ntype I serine/threonine kinase", penwidth=2.2];
        BMPR2    [label="BMPR2 / ActRIIA / ActRIIB\ntype II receptors (constitutively active)"];
        RCOMPLEX [label="Active receptor complex\nBMP9·ALK1·BMPR2·ENG", penwidth=2.2, fillcolor="#d5f5e3"];
        ALK5     [label="ALK5 / TGF-beta pathway\nSMAD2/3 · competing branch"];
        ALK1AG   [label="Restoring the ALK1 pathway (hypothesis)\ntacrolimus · ALK1 agonists\n= the only causal upstream treatment", fillcolor="#f4ecf7"];

        BMP9 -> PROD_BMP [dir=both, color="#2471a3"];
        BMP9 -> RCOMPLEX [color="#1a7f37"];
        BMP10 -> RCOMPLEX [color="#1a7f37"];
        ENG_PROT -> RCOMPLEX [color="#1a7f37", label="amplification"];
        ALK1 -> RCOMPLEX [color="#1a7f37"];
        BMPR2 -> RCOMPLEX [color="#1a7f37"];
        SENG -> BMP9 [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, label="scavenging"];
        RCOMPLEX -> ALK5 [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, style=dashed];
        ALK1AG -> RCOMPLEX [color="#8e44ad", style=dashed, penwidth=1.5];
    }
    G_ENG -> ENG_PROT [color="#1a7f37", lhead=cluster_recept];
    G_ACVRL1 -> ALK1 [color="#1a7f37"];
    G_GDF2 -> BMP9 [color="#1a7f37"];
    LESEC -> RCOMPLEX [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.8, label="biallelic loss"];

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 3. SMAD1/5/8 transcriptional output                                  *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_smad {
        label=<<b>3. SMAD1/5/8 phosphorylation · transcriptional output</b><br/><font point-size="9">the quiescence program</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#eafaf1"; color="#a9dfbf"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#e8f8f0"];

        PSMAD    [label="pSMAD1/5/8 activity\n= lesion signalling state variables PS_n/g/h/p/c", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#d5f5e3"];
        SMAD4P   [label="SMAD4 (common mediator)\nnuclear translocation partner", penwidth=2.2];
        ID1      [label="ID1 transcript\nthe canonical readout gene", penwidth=2.2];
        HEY_HES  [label="HEY1/HEY2 · HES1\narterial identity programme"];
        SMAD67   [label="SMAD6 / SMAD7\ninhibitory feedback"];
        ENG_TX   [label="ENG · ACVRL1 autoinduction\n(the pathway maintains its own receptors)"];
        JAG_DLL  [label="DLL4 / JAG1\nNotch ligand transcription"];
        QUIESC   [label="Endothelial quiescence phenotype\nlow proliferation · low migration · tight junctions kept", penwidth=2.2, fillcolor="#d5f5e3"];

        RCOMPLEX -> PSMAD [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.8];
        PSMAD -> SMAD4P [color="#1a7f37"];
        SMAD4P -> ID1 [color="#1a7f37"];
        SMAD4P -> HEY_HES [color="#1a7f37"];
        SMAD4P -> SMAD67 [color="#1a7f37"];
        SMAD67 -> PSMAD [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, style=dashed, label="negative feedback"];
        SMAD4P -> ENG_TX [color="#1a7f37"];
        ENG_TX -> ENG_PROT [color="#1a7f37", style=dashed];
        SMAD4P -> JAG_DLL [color="#1a7f37"];
        SMAD4P -> QUIESC [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.6];
        G_SMAD4 -> SMAD4P [color="#1a7f37"];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 4. Shear stress mechanotransduction — normal set point               *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_mech {
        label=<<b>4. Shear stress mechanotransduction — the normal set point circuit</b><br/><font point-size="9">PECAM1/VEGFR2/VE-cadherin → SMAD1/5 (PMID 27646277 · 32078368)</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#fef5e7"; color="#f5cba7"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#fdf2e2"];

        WSS      [label="Wall shear stress WSS\nWSS ∝ Q/S³", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#fae5d3"];
        MECHSENS [label="Mechanosensory complex\nPECAM1 · VE-cadherin · VEGFR2\nPlexinD1 · Piezo1"];
        LPHN2    [label="Latrophilin-2 / Shank3\nflow-dependent SMAD1/5 activation"];
        CX37     [label="Connexin37 (Cx37)\ndownstream of shear · flow alignment"];
        KLF2     [label="KLF2 / KLF4\nlaminar flow response transcription factors"];
        SETPOINT [label="Shear stress set point\nnormal: WSS↑ → inward remodelling → WSS returns\n(negative feedback)", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#d5f5e3"];
        INWARD   [label="Inward remodelling\nlumen narrows · self-limiting", fillcolor="#d5f5e3"];
        ALIGN    [label="Endothelial flow alignment\ncell polarity · direction of migration"];

        WSS -> MECHSENS [color="#b03a2e", penwidth=1.8];
        MECHSENS -> PSMAD [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.8, label="shear-dependent amplification"];
        LPHN2 -> PSMAD [color="#1a7f37", style=dashed];
        MECHSENS -> KLF2 [color="#1a7f37"];
        PSMAD -> CX37 [color="#1a7f37"];
        CX37 -> ALIGN [color="#1a7f37"];
        PSMAD -> SETPOINT [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.8];
        SETPOINT -> INWARD [color="#1a7f37"];
        INWARD -> WSS [color="#b03a2e", arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.8, label="return to set point"];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 5. ★ The sign flip — the centre of this map                          *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_flip {
        label=<<b>5. ★ THE SIGN FLIP</b><br/><font point-size="9">REMOD = KSH · g(WSS) · (1 − 2·pSMAD_rel)</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#fdedec"; color="#e6b0aa"; fontsize=12;
        node [fillcolor="#fadbd8"];

        SIGNTERM [label="Remodelling term\nREMOD = KSH·g(WSS)·(1 − 2·pSMAD_rel)", penwidth=2.6, fillcolor="#f5b7b1"];
        NORMBR   [label="pSMAD_rel = 1 (normal)\nREMOD < 0 → inward remodelling\nself-limiting · no lesion", fillcolor="#d5f5e3"];
        LESBR    [label="pSMAD_rel ≈ 0.03 (second hit)\nREMOD > 0 → outward remodelling\nself-amplifying · lesion enlarges", fillcolor="#f5b7b1", penwidth=2.2];
        FEEDER   [label="Feeder vessel resistance limit\nWSS ∝ S/(1+(S/S_feed)⁴)\nshear stress does not rise monotonically", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#fdebd0"];
        BASIN_T  [label="Basin 1 — telangiectasia\narteriolar supply → shear saturates early\nstable lumen · reachable by drug", penwidth=2.2, fillcolor="#d4efdf"];
        BASIN_A  [label="Basin 2 — arteriovenous malformation (AVM)\nconducting artery supply → shear never saturates\na drug-refractory floor exists", penwidth=2.2, fillcolor="#f5b7b1"];
        OUTWARD  [label="Outward remodelling\nlumen enlarges · wall thins", penwidth=2.2];

        SIGNTERM -> NORMBR [color="#1a7f37"];
        SIGNTERM -> LESBR [color="#c0392b", penwidth=1.8];
        LESBR -> OUTWARD [color="#c0392b", penwidth=1.8];
        FEEDER -> BASIN_T [color="#1a7f37"];
        FEEDER -> BASIN_A [color="#c0392b"];
        OUTWARD -> BASIN_T [style=dashed];
        OUTWARD -> BASIN_A [style=dashed];
        NORMBR -> INWARD [color="#1a7f37", style=dashed];
    }
    PSMAD -> SIGNTERM [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=2.0, label="sets the sign"];
    WSS -> SIGNTERM [color="#b03a2e", penwidth=2.0];
    WSS -> FEEDER [color="#b03a2e"];

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 6. PI3K/AKT · VEGF signalling (angiogenic drive)                     *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_vegf {
        label=<<b>6. VEGF-A · VEGFR2 · PI3K/AKT — the angiogenic drive</b><br/><font point-size="9">the drive that bevacizumab and pazopanib remove</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#f4ecf7"; color="#d2b4de"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#eee3f5"];

        VEGFA    [label="Tissue VEGF-A\nrises when pSMAD is lost\n(PMID 15951295)", penwidth=2.4];
        VEGFR1   [label="VEGFR1 (Flt-1)\ndecoy receptor · expression reduced in HHT\n(PMID 30571259)", fillcolor="#fdedec"];
        VEGFR2   [label="VEGFR2 (KDR)\nthe main signalling receptor", penwidth=2.2];
        VEGFFREE [label="Free VEGF-A\n= total VEGF − bevacizumab-bound", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#e8daef"];
        PI3K     [label="PI3K / AKT\nnormally restrained by pSMAD", penwidth=2.4];
        MTOR     [label="mTORC1\nendothelial proliferation · size"];
        ERK      [label="ERK1/2\nproliferative signal"];
        ENOS     [label="eNOS / NO\nvasodilatation · permeability"];
        ANG2     [label="Angiopoietin-2 (ANGPT2)\nTie2 antagonism · mural cell detachment"];
        TIE2     [label="Tie2 / ANGPT1\nthe vessel stabilisation axis"];
        MMP9     [label="MMP-2 / MMP-9\nbasement membrane degradation · sENG generation"];
        ANGIO    [label="Angiogenesis index ANGIO\n= VEGF signal × AKT / (1+2.2·pSMAD)", penwidth=2.6, fillcolor="#e8daef"];
        PROLIF   [label="Endothelial proliferation · migration\nsprouting · luminal enlargement"];
        HYPOX    [label="Hypoxia (HIF-1α)\npulmonary shunt → SpO2↓ → VEGF↑", fillcolor="#fdf2e9"];

        VEGFA -> VEGFFREE [color="#2471a3"];
        VEGFFREE -> VEGFR2 [color="#1a7f37"];
        VEGFR1 -> VEGFFREE [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, label="decoy"];
        VEGFR2 -> PI3K [color="#1a7f37"];
        VEGFR2 -> ERK [color="#1a7f37"];
        PI3K -> MTOR [color="#1a7f37"];
        PI3K -> ENOS [color="#1a7f37"];
        PSMAD -> PI3K [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.6];
        PSMAD -> VEGFA [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.6];
        PSMAD -> VEGFR1 [color="#1a7f37", style=dashed];
        VEGFR2 -> ANGIO [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.6];
        PI3K -> ANGIO [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.6];
        ANGIO -> PROLIF [color="#1a7f37"];
        ANGIO -> ANG2 [color="#1a7f37"];
        ANG2 -> TIE2 [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        ANGIO -> MMP9 [color="#1a7f37"];
        MMP9 -> SENG [color="#1a7f37", style=dashed];
        HYPOX -> VEGFA [color="#1a7f37"];
        PROLIF -> OUTWARD [color="#c0392b"];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 7. Mural cell (pericyte/SMC) coverage — determinant of fragility     *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_mural {
        label=<<b>7. Mural cell coverage — the determinant of bleeding fragility</b><br/><font point-size="9">PDGF-B / PDGFRβ · the target of the thalidomide class (PMID 20364125)</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#e8f6f3"; color="#a2d9ce"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#dff2ee"];

        PDGFB    [label="Endothelial PDGF-B\nmural cell recruitment signal", penwidth=2.4];
        PDGFRB   [label="Pericyte PDGFRβ\nthe recruitment receptor", penwidth=2.2];
        PERICYTE [label="Pericytes / vascular smooth muscle\nmechanical support of the vessel wall"];
        MURAL    [label="Mural cell coverage MU\nnormal ~0.80 · lesion ~0.52", penwidth=2.6, fillcolor="#a9dfbf"];
        BM       [label="Basement membrane thickness · collagen IV\ntensile support"];
        FRAG     [label="Vessel fragility FRAG\n= (1 − MU)^1.55", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#fadbd8"];
        MATURE   [label="Vessel maturation (the inward maturation term)\nKMAT·MU → lumen narrows"];
        TJ       [label="Endothelial tight junctions\nVE-cadherin · claudin-5"];

        PSMAD -> PDGFB [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.6];
        PDGFB -> PDGFRB [color="#1a7f37"];
        PDGFRB -> PERICYTE [color="#1a7f37"];
        PERICYTE -> MURAL [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.6];
        MURAL -> BM [color="#1a7f37"];
        MURAL -> FRAG [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.8, label="coverage↑ → fragility↓"];
        MURAL -> MATURE [color="#1a7f37"];
        MATURE -> INWARD [color="#1a7f37", style=dashed];
        ANGIO -> MURAL [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, label="mural cell detachment"];
        ANG2 -> PERICYTE [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        MURAL -> TJ [color="#1a7f37"];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 8. Arteriovenous identity · Notch                                    *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_av {
        label=<<b>8. Arteriovenous identity · loss of the capillary bed</b><br/><font point-size="9">arteriovenous identity → direct shunt</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#fbeee6"; color="#edbb99"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#fae5d7"];

        NOTCH    [label="Notch1 / DLL4\nmaintains arterial identity"];
        EFNB2    [label="EphrinB2 (arterial marker)"];
        EPHB4    [label="EphB4 (venous marker)"];
        AVIDENT  [label="Loss of the arteriovenous boundary\narterial and venous markers intermingled"];
        CAPLOSS  [label="Loss of the interposed capillary bed\n= the anatomical definition of a shunt", penwidth=2.2, fillcolor="#f5b7b1"];
        DIRECTAV [label="Direct arteriovenous connection\nresistance collapses · flow surges", penwidth=2.2, fillcolor="#f5b7b1"];

        JAG_DLL -> NOTCH [color="#1a7f37"];
        NOTCH -> EFNB2 [color="#1a7f37"];
        PSMAD -> AVIDENT [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        NOTCH -> AVIDENT [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        AVIDENT -> CAPLOSS [color="#c0392b"];
        EPHB4 -> AVIDENT [style=dashed];
        CAPLOSS -> DIRECTAV [color="#c0392b", penwidth=1.6];
        DIRECTAV -> WSS [color="#b03a2e", penwidth=1.8, label="flow↑"];
        OUTWARD -> CAPLOSS [color="#c0392b", style=dashed];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 9. Lesion population — number · size · regression                    *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_lesion {
        label=<<b>9. Lesion population dynamics — number N, mean lumen S</b><br/><font point-size="9">severity tracks lesion NUMBER; calibre has a stable fixed point</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#fdedec"; color="#e6b0aa"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#fbe3e1"];

        NLES     [label="Lesion number N_n / N_g\naccumulates over decades with age", penwidth=2.6, fillcolor="#f5b7b1"];
        SLES     [label="Mean lumen S_n / S_g\nstable fixed point ≈ 2.3-3.6", penwidth=2.6, fillcolor="#f5b7b1"];
        BIRTH    [label="Lesion birth rate\nKHIT·SEV·Hill(ANGIO_field)"];
        INVOL    [label="Lesion involution\naccelerates once the drive is removed\n(PMID 34910078 skin lesions disappear)", fillcolor="#d4efdf"];
        DILUT    [label="Mean-dilution term\nnew lesions enter at S_BIRTH"];
        SMAXA    [label="Anatomical ceiling SMAX\nmucosa 6 · gut 7.5 · liver 48"];
        AGEACC   [label="Age-dependent accumulation\n1/KREG ≈ 30-year time constant\n→ plateau in the fifties and sixties", fillcolor="#fdf2e9"];

        BIRTH -> NLES [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.6];
        INVOL -> NLES [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.6];
        ANGIO -> BIRTH [color="#1a7f37"];
        ANGIO -> INVOL [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, label="drive removed → involution"];
        SOMHIT -> BIRTH [color="#2471a3"];
        SIGNTERM -> SLES [color="#c0392b", penwidth=1.8];
        ANGIO -> SLES [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.6];
        MATURE -> SLES [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        DILUT -> SLES [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        BIRTH -> DILUT [style=dashed];
        SMAXA -> SLES [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        NLES -> AGEACC [color="#e67e22", style=dashed];
        SLES -> WSS [color="#b03a2e", penwidth=1.8, label="size → shear"];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 10. Nasal mucosa · epistaxis                                         *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_nose {
        label=<<b>10. Nasal mucosal lesions · epistaxis</b><br/><font point-size="9">95% of patients · the dominant symptom</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#fef9e7"; color="#f7dc6f"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#fdf6e3"];

        NASMUC   [label="Septal · Little's area mucosa\ntrauma exposure · dryness · airflow"];
        NASTEL   [label="Nasal telangiectasia\ndilated submucosal venous plexus"];
        NASTRAUM [label="Mucosal trauma · dryness · crusting\nthe bleed-triggering event"];
        EVRATE   [label="Bleeding event frequency\n= KE_N · N_n · FRAG", penwidth=2.2];
        EVDUR    [label="Duration per event (min)\n= TEV·S·(1+2.6·(1−MU))·lysis factor", penwidth=2.2];
        EVRATE2  [label="Bleeding rate per event (mL/min)\n= RBLD·S²  (gush intensity)", penwidth=2.2];
        EVVOL    [label="Blood loss per event (mL)\n= rate × duration", penwidth=2.2];
        BLRN     [label="Nasal bleeding rate BLR_N (mL/day)", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#fadbd8"];
        MED      [label="Monthly epistaxis duration MED\n(min/month) — the FDA-preferred endpoint", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#f9e79f"];

        NASMUC -> NASTEL [style=dashed];
        NLES -> NASTEL [color="#2471a3"];
        NASTRAUM -> EVRATE [color="#1a7f37"];
        FRAG -> EVRATE [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.6];
        NLES -> EVRATE [color="#1a7f37", penwidth=1.6];
        SLES -> EVDUR [color="#1a7f37"];
        SLES -> EVRATE2 [color="#1a7f37"];
        MURAL -> EVDUR [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        EVRATE2 -> EVVOL [color="#2471a3"];
        EVDUR -> EVVOL [color="#2471a3"];
        EVRATE -> BLRN [color="#2471a3", penwidth=1.6];
        EVVOL -> BLRN [color="#2471a3", penwidth=1.6];
        EVRATE -> MED [color="#e67e22"];
        EVDUR -> MED [color="#e67e22"];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 11. Gastrointestinal angiodysplasia                                  *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_gi {
        label=<<b>11. Gastrointestinal angiodysplasia — continuous oozing haemorrhage</b><br/><font point-size="9">25-30% of patients; the reason some become transfusion-dependent</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#fef9e7"; color="#f7dc6f"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#fdf6e3"];

        GITEL    [label="Gastric · small bowel telangiectasia\nmultiple · diagnosed endoscopically"];
        GIOOZE   [label="Continuous ooze (uninterrupted bleeding)\n= KGB·N_g·FRAG·S_g³", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#fadbd8"];
        GIOCC    [label="Occult blood · asymptomatic chronic loss\n(anaemia is possible without epistaxis)"];
        BLRG     [label="Gastrointestinal bleeding rate BLR_G (mL/day)", penwidth=2.4, fillcolor="#fadbd8"];
        BLRTOT   [label="Total bleeding rate BLR (mL/day)\n= BLR_N + BLR_G", penwidth=2.6, fillcolor="#f5b7b1"];

        NLES -> GITEL [style=dashed];
        GITEL -> GIOOZE [color="#2471a3"];
        FRAG -> GIOOZE [color="#1a7f37"];
        GIOOZE -> BLRG [color="#2471a3", penwidth=1.6];
        GIOOZE -> GIOCC [color="#e67e22"];
        BLRG -> BLRTOT [color="#2471a3", penwidth=1.8];
        BLRN -> BLRTOT [color="#2471a3", penwidth=1.8];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 12. Haemostasis · fibrinolysis                                       *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_hemo {
        label=<<b>12. Haemostasis · fibrinolysis — the one point tranexamic acid touches</b><br/><font point-size="9">TXA moves duration, not episode count (PMID 25040799)</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#eaf2f8"; color="#aed6f1"; fontsize=11;
        node [fillcolor="#e2edf8"];

        PLGN     [label="Plasminogen"];
        TPA      [label="tPA / uPA\nhigh local activity in the mucosa"];
        PLASMIN  [label="Plasmin activity PLG", penwidth=2.4];
        FIBRIN   [label="Fibrin clot"];
        CLOTSTAB [label="Clot stability\n= 1/(1 + FLYS·PLG)", penwidth=2.2];
        LYSSHARE [label="Lysis contribution FLYS = 0.256\n→ theoretical ceiling of complete antifibrinolysis −20.4%", fillcolor="#fdf2e9", penwidth=2.2];
        PLTFN    [label="Platelet function (normal)\nHHT is not a coagulopathy", fillcolor="#eaeded"];
        VWF      [label="von Willebrand factor (normal)"];

        PLGN -> PLASMIN [color="#1a7f37"];
        TPA -> PLASMIN [color="#1a7f37"];
        PLASMIN -> FIBRIN [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        FIBRIN -> CLOTSTAB [color="#1a7f37"];
        PLASMIN -> CLOTSTAB [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.6];
        CLOTSTAB -> EVDUR [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.6];
        CLOTSTAB -> EVVOL [color="#c0392b", arrowhead=tee];
        LYSSHARE -> CLOTSTAB [style=dashed];
        PLTFN -> FIBRIN [color="#1a7f37", style=dashed];
        VWF -> PLTFN [style=dashed];
    }

    /* ================================================================== *
     * 13. Hepatic AVM · high-output heart failure                          *
     * ================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_liver {
        label=<<b>13. Hepatic vascular malformation — the high-output heart failure route</b><br/><font point-size="9">~74% of HHT2; the AVM basin (PMID 22396517)</font>>;
        style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#f9ebea"; color="#e6b0aa"; fontsize=11;
